    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "DNR order:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " placed in the medical record by a clinician; it tells the medical staff that CPR should not be done in the event of cardiac arrest."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Surrogates:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " if the patient is incapable of deciding about CPR, a surrogate may decide based on the patient’s previously expressed preferences or, if those are unknown, the patient’s best interests."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Outside the hospital:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " first responders are almost always required to start life support unless a valid DNR order or portable medical order (often called a POLST form) is in place and presented to them."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "POLST:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a set of medical orders, portable across all health care settings, that addresses CPR, overall goals of treatment (comfort care only, full curative treatment, or limited treatment in between) and usually other critical care decisions such as artificial nutrition and hydration."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Who qualifies for POLST:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " the most common criterion is that the clinician would not be surprised if the patient were to die within the next year or two."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
